== -1) or after only the\n+\t// headers have been written (size == 0), but reject it once body data has\n+\t// been written (size > 0) to avoid corrupting the response.\n+\tif w.size > 0 {\n \t\treturn nil, nil, errHijackAlreadyWritten\n \t}\n \tif w.size < 0 {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017ZqFiPQtzqxSCKwLnzvhbH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
